.TH LAMBOOT\-CAPCHECK 1 "2026-06-03" "lamboot-tools" "lamboot-tools Manual"
.SH NAME
lamboot\-capcheck \- firmware and platform capability auditor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lamboot\-capcheck
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fITOKENS\fR]...
.br
.B lamboot\-capcheck
.B audit
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B lamboot\-capcheck
.B \-\-json
.B audit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lamboot\-capcheck
is a vendor\-neutral firmware and platform capability auditor for Linux
hosts. It discovers what a machine's firmware and platform
.I claim
to support, verifies which of those claims actually hold up, cross\-references
a curated quirks database, and reports the result for humans or machines.
It audits twelve firmware and platform domains, reading
.IR /sys ,
.IR /proc ,
the ESP, and (with the invasive options) UEFI runtime variables.
.PP
This binary is a prebuilt, statically linked component of the lamboot\-tools
suite. The shell tools
.BR lamboot\-doctor (1)
and
.BR lamboot\-migrate (1)
consume it automatically when it is present on
.BR PATH :
lamboot\-doctor splices its findings into the unified diagnostic report, and
lamboot\-migrate's optional
.B \-\-capcheck\-gate
refuses an unsafe migration when a critical firmware quirk is detected. Both
degrade gracefully when this binary is absent.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B audit
Run the capability audit across all enabled domains.
.TP
.B help \fR[\fINAME\fR]
Print the inline registry, or deep\-dive a subcommand, domain, or check.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: \fBhuman\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBjunit\-xml\fR,
\fBmarkdown\fR, \fBcsv\fR, or \fBsarif\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Shorthand for \fB\-\-format json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-target\-root " " \fIPATH\fR
Treat \fIPATH\fR as the filesystem root (offline analysis of a mounted target).
.TP
.BR \-\-offline\-bundle " " \fIPATH\fR
Read inputs from a bundle directory or tarball instead of live
.IR /sys .
.TP
.B \-\-lamboot
Enable the optional LamBoot\-integration add\-on checks.
.TP
.BR \-\-redact ", " \-\-no\-redact
Redact or force inclusion of PII (serials, MACs, UUIDs).
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Treat WARN findings as FAIL.
.TP
.B \-\-exit\-on\-fail
Exit nonzero if any check reports FAIL.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output (repeatable: \fB\-vv\fR for trace).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Audit completed (see findings for verdicts).
.TP
.B nonzero
With \fB\-\-exit\-on\-fail\fR or \fB\-\-strict\fR, indicates a FAIL\-severity finding.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys, /proc
Live firmware and platform state.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/lamboot-tools/lamboot-capcheck.THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
License notices for the bundled Rust dependencies.
.SH SOURCE
The source for this component lives in its own repository,
.UR https://github.com/lamco-admin/lamboot-capcheck
.UE .
The binary shipped here is built static against musl for cross\-distribution
portability and vendored into the lamboot\-tools release.
